description:
Closes #316. Closes #374.

Example app (container div is shaded yellow):

``` R
library(shiny)
library(ggvis)

shinyApp(
  ui = fluidPage(
    div(style = "width:300px; height:300px; background: #ffd;",
      ggvisOutput("plot")
    )
  ),
  server = function(input, output) {
    mtcars %>% ggvis(~wt, ~mpg) %>% layer_points() %>%
      set_options(width = "auto", height = "auto", resizable=FALSE) %>%
      bind_shiny("plot")
  }
)
```

This app demonstrates how the height and width settings interact work when the wrapper div has a specified size:

``` R
library(shiny)
library(ggvis)

shinyApp(
  ui = fluidPage(sidebarLayout(
    sidebarPanel(
      radioButtons("width", "Width", c("auto", "400")),
      radioButtons("height", "Height", c("auto", "400")),
      radioButtons("resizable", "Resizable (enabled only if width and height are fixed)",
                   c("Yes", "No"))
    ),
    mainPanel(
      div(style = "width:300px; height:300px; background: #ffd;",
        ggvisOutput("plot")
      )
    )
  )),
  server = function(input, output) {
    reactive({
      resizable <- (input$resizable == "Yes")

      mtcars %>% ggvis(~wt, ~mpg) %>% layer_points() %>%
      set_options(width = input$width, height = input$height, resizable=resizable)
    }) %>%
      bind_shiny("plot")
  }
)
```
